# Billing — Signup registrations (UC-110, UC-127)
# Reserved before the tenant exists, so the Google sub, tax id and terms never travel through
# Pub/Sub or the audit log. Tenant-less route under /internal/*, InternalApiGuard only.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev
#
# REST Client environment: select "local" in VS Code status bar

@baseUrl     = {{backendUrl}}
@internalKey = {{$dotenv INTERNAL_API_KEY}}

### Self-signup (BFF). trialAvailable false => no row was inserted and registrationId is null.
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/billing/registrations
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "source": "SELF_SIGNUP",
  "googleSub": "112233445566778899001",
  "taxId": "529.982.247-25",
  "countryCode": "BR",
  "terms": { "version": "2026-11-01" }
}

###

### Operator (scripts/provision-tenant.sh): no lock, no eligibility check, always a fresh row.
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/billing/registrations
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "source": "OPERATOR",
  "taxId": "11.222.333/0001-81",
  "countryCode": "BR"
}

###

### Invalid: a self-signup without terms → 422 SIGNUP_TERMS_NOT_ACCEPTED
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/billing/registrations
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "SELF_SIGNUP", "googleSub": "112233445566778899001" }

###

### Invalid: a taxId without countryCode → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/billing/registrations
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "OPERATOR", "taxId": "529.982.247-25" }
